          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Etching is the price of owning marble, and it is fixable. Confirm it is an etch rather than a stain, polish light marks on polished stone with a purpose-made compound, blend marks on honed stone with fine abrasives, and leave large or deep damage to a restoration professional. Reseal any area you have polished or honed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then prevent the next one with quick wiping, coasters, trays and a pH-neutral cleaner. Keep the stone sealed with a good product from our <a href="/best-marble-sealer/">marble sealer guide</a> as well. It will not stop acids, but it stops the stains that so often come with them.
